+# ROLAX duplicate-message fix — Vercel deployment
+
+This package contains the existing ROLAX website source plus the webhook fix.
+It does not contain bot tokens, API keys, SSH keys, `.env` files, `.vercel`, or user data.
+
+## Deploy to the existing project
+
+Run these commands from the unzipped folder:
+
+```bash
+npm install
+npx vercel login
+npx vercel link --project rolax-web-hosting
+npx vercel --prod
+```
+
+When Vercel asks whether to link to an existing project, choose:
+
+```text
+rolax-web-hosting
+```
+
+Do not create a new project. Existing production environment variables must remain unchanged.
+
+## Verify after deployment
+
+1. Open `https://rolax-web-hosting.vercel.app/api/rolax_webhook` and confirm it returns the ROLAX webhook JSON response.
+2. Send one test message to `@ROLAXHOSTINGv2bot`.
+3. Confirm exactly one reply arrives.
+4. Send a second different message and confirm exactly one reply arrives again.
+5. Test one admin button/callback and confirm it also replies only once.
+
+The fix claims each Telegram `update_id` before the handler runs, keeps a short encrypted retry window across cold starts/redeploys, and does not retry uncertain Telegram send failures. Existing user records, plans, expiries, bans, restrictions, credits, referrals, metadata, force-join entries, and encrypted state are preserved.
